# Context own default that is root-unordered — a recorded besluit-6 flank

Besluit 6's generated highest default forces a reentrant callee target's own
default to a **base default** so a caller override can ride above it. That works for a
CHAIN own default. When the callee's own default is itself a **root-level
unordered** group (two unordered grounds, no unconditional base), there is no
single base for a highest default to sit above: it stays refused loudly, one of the
narrowed remnants of the old blanket context refusal (CONSTRUCTS row 9 /
`spec/proposals/PHASE5-CATALA.md` decision 6).

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  context drempel content integer
  output uitkomst content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition drempel under condition grondslag >= 10 consequence equals 10
  definition drempel under condition grondslag <= 5 consequence equals 20
  definition uitkomst equals grondslag - drempel

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslag content integer
  kamer scope Kamer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition kamer.grondslag equals grondslag
  definition heffing equals kamer.uitkomst
```
